class:: TStableRand
summary:: Triggered alpha-stable sampler in Nolan S0 parameterization
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic>Distributions
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/TCauchyRand, Classes/TGaussRand

description::

Samples Nolan's S0 alpha-stable parameterization with the Chambers–Mallows–Stuck construction and a separate alpha-one form. Parameterizations are not interchangeable: this class is specifically S0.

Alpha 2 is Gaussian under this parameterization; alpha 1 with beta 0 is Cauchy. Moments may not exist, and extreme finite values are expected and may require explicit user-side limiting before direct audio use.

Like link::Classes/TGaussRand::, alpha 2 produces Gaussian-shaped draws; unlike it, TStableRand spans skewed heavy-tailed stable laws with a local resettable seed.

subsection:: Stable-family shape

image::stable-density.png#Smoothed empirical S0 densities with beta = 0, scale = 1, and alpha = 2, 1.5, and 1, shown in muted teal, blue, and plum over a finite display interval. Smaller alpha makes the center sharper and the tails heavier.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: alpha
Stability exponent, clipped to 0.01 through 2.
argument:: beta
Skew parameter, clipped to -1 through 1.
argument:: scale
Scale magnitude.
argument:: location
S0 location.
argument:: trig
Resample on a rising edge.
argument:: seed
Init-rate local seed.
argument:: reset
Restore the seed and sample a new initial value.
argument:: mul
Output multiplier.
argument:: add
Output offset.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ TStableRand.kr(1.5, 0, 1, 0, Impulse.kr(4)).poll }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar(TStableRand.kr(1.8, 0, 300, 800, Impulse.kr(8)).clip(80, 4000), 0, 0.08) }.play
)
::

